# Build context hygiene. Both images COPY only pyproject.toml, app/, web/,
# migrations/, playbooks/ and tests/ -- but the context is the repo root, which
# carries the 726 MB SFTP corpus and a 44 MB .git. Without this file every
# `docker compose build` uploaded ~2 GB to the daemon before running a single
# instruction (measured 2026-08-20 on a `build web` that was still streaming
# context after several minutes).
#
# Keep in step with the COPY lines in Dockerfile / Dockerfile.web: this is a
# deny list, so a NEW build input is included automatically and only needs
# attention here if it lives under a path named below.

# The document corpus and its outputs -- mounted at runtime, never baked in.
imports/
archive/
analysis-out/
# Database dumps written by scripts/deploy.sh.
backups/

# Secrets must never enter a build context, COPYed or not.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/
docs/
tasks/
*.md
!README.md

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
venv/

*.log
.claude/
